tructure I used to raise CQ5's conjunct A from 0.283 to 0.35 and would make the compressed-start evidence (MOVE ~59-71 in late 2025 / 2026, LR 0.80 after overlap haircut) worthless. CQ5 rises from 26 toward ~38; my CQ4 P50 moves up ~0.3pp toward 2.45 and the P90 toward 3.8; CQ6-C gains ~4 at B's expense. The reverse — MOVE averaging below 85 across 2027-2029 — drops CQ5 to ~15.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Eurostat Structure of Earnings Survey (the 2030 wave, published ~2032-33) shows real median hourly earnings growth in ISIC Q exceeding ISIC J by more than 5.0pp cumulatively since the 2026 wave, in at least five of the EU's largest member states.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"Falsifies the two mechanisms carrying my CQ1 down to 8 — administered-price suppression of care wages and the median-vs-share composition trap (LRs 0.70 and 0.60). CQ1 rises from 8 to ~22-25 (conjunct 2 from 0.11 to ~0.35); it also raises CQ6-C by ~3 via the care-wage channel into core services, and raises my score on hypothesis plank (a) from 5 to ~20. This is the cheapest available test of my seat's largest downward update, and it resolves on an administrative release rather than on telemetry.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 2 bayes seat, effort 'inflation'."}}